{"id": "tech-4", "headline": "Threads arrives on iPad with stock cashtags", "source": "TechCrunch", "url": "https://techcrunch.com/2026/11/24/threads-comes-to-ipad-and-takes-a-page-from-xs-playbook-with-cashtags/", "published": "2026-11-24", "url_verified": true, "pages": ["Meta's Threads has launched an iPad app in an overnight update, taking less time to reach the tablet than Instagram did. The app works well in portrait, but some users are disappointed that landscape mode uses a single-column feed instead of the multi-column layout of the web app. Swiping left or right opens the feeds menu and search. The release also adds cashtags, a feature popularized by Twitter. Tags start with a dollar sign and a ticker symbol, and tapping one opens discussion about that stock. Threads will show live quotes, charts and other context at the top of each cashtag page, and autocomplete suggestions appear when searching for one. Source: TechCrunch."], "qr": {"n": 37, "rows": ["1111111001001100100110011010001111111", "1000001011000111001011100011001000001", "1011101001010010001011110000001011101", "1011101011011111010100111101101011101", "1011101000011100101100010100001011101", "1000001010100111101011001111101000001", "1111111010101010101010101010101111111", "0000000000011011000001100010100000000", "1111101111100110110000100110010101010", "0001110110010100101111110010000001110", "0000011011100101110011000011110001101", "1001010111010011000011000001000011010", "0001011000001101010100111111111011101", "1101100001110100101101011100000100110", "1110101010100011000011000001101110111", "1101100000001011100101111001010001001", "1001011110101110011010100111111011101", "0100110100010010111111010010000100110", "0110011000101111000011100101110010111", "1101110010000011000011000000110110001", "0000111000000111110000001110011010111", "0011100110010100101110010000000100010", "0011101101101001110011100011010101011", "0100110010001011101101100010111100001", "0001111001011110010100111111101111111"